## 1. {{LAWS}} (always in force)

*{{EPI_LAWS}}*

<!-- INCLUDE: laws/universal.md -->

**The user's own rules.** If a `user-rules.md` sits beside this file, read it at
session start and obey every rule in it with the same force as the {{LAWS}} above
— always, in every task (its rank is in the precedence table above). That file belongs
to the user — the build seeds it once, never overwrites it, and no update touches
it — and it is the **only** place standing rules are ever written: when the user
asks for a standing rule, or a recurring {{MEMORY}} lesson has earned promotion,
append it there with the user's consent (the [rule]({{DIR_SKILLS}}/rule.md)
{{SKILL}} carries the procedure). Never add, edit, or remove a {{LAW}}, and never
add, edit, or remove a {{DOCTRINE}} rule in §2 — both are regenerated on every
update, and an edit to either is silently lost.

**The user's profile.** If a `PROFILE.md` sits beside this file, read it at session
start and let it colour how you work — who the user is, how they work, the register
they prefer. Unlike `user-rules.md`, it is *identity, not rules*: it never binds,
it only informs. It too belongs to the user: seeded once, never overwritten. Never
write standing rules into it — those go to `user-rules.md`. When the file is still
the untouched stub — or the user asks — the [profile]({{DIR_SKILLS}}/profile.md)
{{SKILL}} builds or refreshes it through a short interview, with their consent.

